  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "In some languages the everyday word for a meal, or for a basic food such as rice or bread, is also the word for food in general. English keeps **food**, **meal**, and the name of the food apart.",
    "grammar": "**Food** is uncountable in general use (*There's no food*) but countable for kinds of food (*new foods*). Translators should not use the plural for food in general.",
